  "title": "One new line never adds creation",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "One new line never adds creation. Let one new point b be added to a near side on one new not-all-equal line through two of its points (any signs; the points may lie on the gluing line). For every gluing line showing six patterns and each of the four census far sides, if the near side has no new knot of up to three points, neither does the new one; with TWO-BIT-SCREEN A's no-loss half, the new knots off b are unchanged too, so creation is unchanged. Proved from ticket A's two-round rule: a knot through b is reached or not according to its local configuration (the gluing line, the line's two points, at most one more class and its far classes), and on every such configuration, checked exhaustively, every knot through b is reached whenever every knot off it is.",
